a first read: HTTP/1.1 200 OK, tag a version
another router over the same file, the tag held: HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified, body false
a write through the first: HTTP/1.1 201 Created
the other connection's next answer: HTTP/1.1 200 OK, a new tag true
the new tag held, on each router: HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified
a raw write through a connection: the other router answers HTTP/1.1 200 OK, a new tag true
the file reopened by a new router, nothing changed since: HTTP/1.1 304 Not Modified
a write after the reopening: HTTP/1.1 201 Created, then HTTP/1.1 200 OK with a new tag true
no two states of the data shared a tag: true
